ng  the instructions in the Stevenson  crystal soap base kit spread the batch  that you create between some small jars  to make small molds be sure the  containers can handle high heat after a  few  your mold will be ready next cut off the  amount of soap you will need to fill the  mold and cut it into smaller bits  microwave them for 30 to 45 seconds take  them out and stir to make sure the soap  is liquid now add color use food color  droplets to mix and match the silicone  molds to get the colors you want next  all you have to do is leave the stove to  cool it might be a little tricky the  first few times you do it if the soap  doesn't set around the edges then when  you remove the soap just wash it to get  rid of the liquid soap residue after 2  to 3 uses you shouldn't have this  problem anymore  happy bath time glitter shoes what their  still being no place like home if  Dorothy hadn't had those glittery shoes  no we think not the only way to ensure  that you always make your way home when  you click those heels is to glitterize  your shoes and now thanks to this  tutorial you can here's what you do  find a pair of white shoes that you like  next take your favorite shade of glitter  stop the toe section of your shoes with  something so that it stays sturdy and  doesn't lose shape mix together the  decoupage and glitter concoction that  you have made you can use as much  glitter as you like the more glitter you  use the more solid your coat will be  move in small sections and work the  decoupage over the entire shoe once your  first coat is done let the glitter dry  for a few hours it is very important  that you don't rush this or you will  accidentally brush off your first coat  when you go in to apply the second  repeat the same steps for the second  coat once the glitter is as thick as you  would like it seal everything with a  layer of JQ podge and let it dry  overnight the next morning you will wake  up to beautiful glittery kicks guess who  remember the childhood game guess who  each player pulled a card with a face on  it the object of the game was to guess  the person that was on your opponent's  card you did this by asking questions  like does your person have glasses  do they have brown hair until you were  able to narrow it down to one person  well if you want to add a personalized  twist to the game add in the faces of  your family and friends it's not as hard  as you might think start out by picking  the friends and family members that you  would like to include cut out everyone's  head and add  names to the bottom of their photos  print out three copies of each photo one  for each player and one for the center  pile paint the black of the birch pieces  and attach the faces to the pegs using  double stick tape measure all your pegs  and line them up on the hole glue each  hinge to the peg then screw the hinges  to the board cut your dowel down into  four pieces  glue two down to the front of the board  to hold your card and voila a  personalized game of guess who this is  the perfect gift for a close friend or  family member  light up the room decorating a room can  make a big difference the difference  between a house and a home is just decor  but interior design can get expensive  especially if you like personalized  items so why not make your own this is  what you will need cardboard letters and  string globe lights first pick the word  that you would like to make into your  sign then cut out one side of each of  the cardboard letters with an exacto  knife in the string lighting package the  light bulb should be sitting in a  cardboard tray use the hole in them to  trace openings into the cardboard  letters trace the circles where you want  the light bulbs to go next  use an exacto knife to cut across the  center of each circle making sure the  cut goes from edge to edge turn over the  cardboard letters and poke through to  make the hole larger now you can put the  light bulbs in each hole and screw on  the backing placing the wires in place  inside the cardboard edges these signs  are the perfect way to add some Flair to  any room from the living room to your  bedroom just take a word that fits and  get to creating kinetic foam sand coke  is delicious we all know that but with  all the coke that people consume it'd be  great if you could use those empty coke  bottles for more than just recycling or  trash well we have found one of the most  fun ways to reuse them first you will  need a kinetic stamp kit from pom-pom  toys take a coke bottle and remove the  label next use an exacto knife to cut  the bottle into three separate sections  one at the base of the bottle neck and  one at the bottom of the body of the  bottle next put the cap back on the  bottle scoop your first color of sand  into the section that you're holding  pass the sand down flip the bottle  / remove the cap and pack a little more  sand in the top now shake the bottle  gently letting the foam slide out of the  bottle it should retain the shape of the  top of the coke bottle next take the  label and place it around the foam and  put the cap on top making your foam look  like the top of a coke bottle repeat the  process with the middle and bottom of  the coke bottle and voila you've got a  foam coke bottle DIY neon slime if you  were born in the 90s then you probably  remember the era of slime and years  after it only got better it doesn't have  to be just any old boring slime you can  make it neon all you need is liquid  starch school glue and food coloring  first mix two parts glue and one part  starch next pour the glue and starch  mixture into a bowl then you can add the  food coloring that you want stir it well  make sure it's completely mixed once it  starts to gel you can mix it with your  hands this is a little easier than with  a spoon if your slime turns out too  liquidy you can add more glue on the  other hand if your slime is too sticky  add starch in the same manner continue  mixing until 